## COMMON QUESTIONS & QUICK ANSWERS

**Q: How do I request annual leave?**  
A: Submit request via HRIS portal at least 3 days in advance; get manager approval; system will show if balance is available.

**Q: What happens if I need to work from home occasionally?**  
A: Hybrid employees can work from home on non-office days with manager awareness. Long-term remote requires VP approval.

**Q: Can I take comp-off instead of overtime pay?**  
A: Yes, if your role is not eligible for overtime pay or upon your request. Comp-off must be taken within 30 days of earning.

**Q: What is the dress code for client meetings?**  
A: More formal than smart casual—collared shirts, blazers, formal trousers, or professional dresses. Your manager will notify you if a meeting requires formal dress.

**Q: How do I report a harassment or safety concern?**  
A: Contact your manager, HR (hr@brightpath.com), or use the anonymous reporting form in the HR portal. The company will investigate and protect you from retaliation.

**Q: How long is my probation period?**  
A: Standard 3 months for regular employees. Performance and cultural fit are evaluated; you'll receive formal feedback at 30, 60, and 90 days.

**Q: What is my learning budget?**  
A: INR 40,000/year for courses, books, certifications, or conferences. Discuss with your manager; approval usually granted if learning is role-relevant.

**Q: What happens if I don't use all my annual leave?**  
A: Up to 5 days can be carried over to the next calendar year; beyond 5 days are forfeited. Sick and casual leave do not carry over.

**Q: When will I get my final settlement after resignation?**  
A: Within 45 days of your last working day. Includes final salary, encashed annual leave, and any deductions (per applicable law).

**Q: Can I access company data after I leave?**  
A: No. All system access is revoked on your last day. Download personal files before your last day.

**Q: Is health insurance coverage maintained during maternity/paternity leave?**  
A: Yes. Health insurance and provident fund contributions continue as normal during approved leave.

